+//! Ferrite: part of a Third-Party Modified Version of the Fraunhofer FDK AAC
+//! Codec Library for Android. Modifications and Rust implementation copyright
+//! © 2025–2026 Jeroen Steenvoorde. Modification notice date: 2026-11-16.
+//! Package: ferrite-aac (package license FDK-AAC); see rust/NOTICE for the full license text.
+//! FPE output boundary and shared-output assembly — skeleton (M1).
+//!
+//! Planned content (roadmap `09`):
+//!
+//! - **M2 (FPE-2.3):** shared-output assembly as **pass-through** of the
+//!   Q31 results into the existing [`crate::aac_enc::psy::ChannelOutput`] /
+//!   [`crate::aac_enc::psy::GroupedOutput`] /
+//!   [`crate::aac_enc::psy::MsOutput`] types — no boundary quantization.
+//!   In the M1 skeleton the delegated Q31 engine already constructs these
+//!   shared types, so assembly is the identity pass-through performed by
+//!   [`super::orchestrate`].
+//! - **M3+ (`docs/fpe/05` §7, active per-kernel only when a float kernel
+//!   lands):** boundary quantization `stored_i32 =
+//!   clamp(round(v_f·2^31), i32::MIN, i32::MAX)` (round-to-nearest, the
+//!   same convention as `energy::map_spectrum_to_q31_into`), Ld vectors
+//!   per the `05` §6.8 guard/floor conventions, integer representation
+//!   fields passed through exactly (ADR-0005), grouped vectors via
+//!   integer regroup of quantized per-window values (`05` §6.7), and the
+//!   f64 spectrum (mutated by the reused TNS) passed through unchanged.
+//!   Invariant guards (`05` §8): finite values, non-negative energies /
+//!   thresholds, saturating clamps, Ld sentinel/floor, grouped stride
+//!   layout; a non-finite value is a loud frame-level finding via the
+//!   existing skip-with-note path, never silent.
+//!
+//! Upstream: `psy_main.cpp:1058-1076/1089-1101/1120-1128/1251-1295`
+//! (`LdDataVector`, output build). Q31 mirrors (read-only):
+//! `psy.rs:1285-1537` (`group_short_channel`, `finish_channel`,
+//! `grouped_ld`, `grouped_ld_clamped`).
+//!
+//! **M1:** no boundary code exists yet — introducing rounding or
+//! rescaling now would violate the pass-through contract (risk R-19);
+//! this module intentionally contains no code.
